st expert raters place it in Lean Republican territory, though two call it a tossup.\n\nYet the money and market signals cut the other way. Garcia has raised nearly as much as De La Cruz, Democratic outside groups have outspent Republican ones, and prediction markets give Garcia roughly a two-in-three chance of winning. The only public poll, sponsored by a Democratic firm, showed the candidates statistically tied in late August. With sparse polling and a volatile new electorate, the race remains genuinely uncertain heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4325, "margin": -0.99}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5895, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6117, "margin": 1.5}]}